      "acceptance": "Primitive, explicit, axiomatic, inductive and operational cases are distinct; Axiom artifact is not an axiom assertion; inherited labels do not force equivalence.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "id": "M01",
      "swu_ids": [
        "M01.1"
      ],
      "title": "Definition forms and classification axes"
    },
    {
      "acceptance": "Invariant to be checked cannot be inserted as an assumption to prove itself; hypothesis is not silently adopted as a premise; an accepted premise is not established truth.",
      "depends_on": [
        "M01"
      ],
      "id": "M02",
      "swu_ids": [
        "M02.1"
      ],
      "title": "Logical roles and assumption discipline"
    },
    {
      "acceptance": "Ill-typed application and unbound symbol diagnosed; same labels retain distinct scope identities; nominal disjoint types cannot manufacture semantic distinction.",
      "depends_on": [
        "M01"
      ],
      "id": "M03",
      "swu_ids": [
        "M03.1"
      ],
      "title": "Signatures, carriers and identity"
    },
    {
      "acceptance": "No guessed meaning for iff, implication, quantification or non-entailment notation; recursive iff is not a least fixed point; unsupported operators remain unresolved.",
      "depends_on": [
        "M02",
        "M03"
      ],
      "id": "M04",
      "swu_ids": [
        "M04.1"
      ],
      "title": "Logical language and fragment boundaries"
    },
    {
      "acceptance": "Missing evidence is not falsehood; empty required population is not a useful distinction proof; operational unknown is not silently made a third truth value; plain-language authority strings are not authentication.",
      "depends_on": [
        "M04"
      ],
      "id": "M05",
      "swu_ids": [
        "M05.1"
      ],
      "title": "Denotation, truth and information state"
    },
    {
